{
  "reel_id": "git_18",
  "title": "How Git Actually Stores Your Code",
  "total_ms": 29495,
  "total_frames": 885,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "git01_hook",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Your project has 1,000 files and 500 commits, but dot git is barely 10 megabytes. How?",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 4992,
      "duration_ms": 4992,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 150,
      "cues": [
        {
          "phrase": "1,000 files",
          "cue": "project_files_spawn",
          "frame": 45
        },
        {
          "phrase": "10 megabytes",
          "cue": "small_size_highlight",
          "frame": 112
        }
      ],
      "wav_path": "/Users/talus/Downloads/youtube_ai/OpenMontage/project_tech/reels/git_18/audio/blocks/git01_hook.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "git02_nemi",
      "speaker": "nemi",
      "text": "Doesn't Git just save a list of text diffs line-by-line? \ud83e\udd14",
      "start_ms": 5052,
      "end_ms": 7932,
      "duration_ms": 2880,
      "start_frame": 152,
      "end_frame": 238,
      "cues": [
        {
          "phrase": "text diffs",
          "cue": "diff_myth_animation",
          "frame": 195
        }
      ],
      "wav_path": "/Users/talus/Downloads/youtube_ai/OpenMontage/project_tech/reels/git_18/audio/blocks/git02_nemi.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "git03_truth",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "No! Git is actually a content-addressable database of immutable snapshots.",
      "start_ms": 7992,
      "end_ms": 12280,
      "duration_ms": 4288,
      "start_frame": 240,
      "end_frame": 368,
      "cues": [
        {
          "phrase": "content-addressable",
          "cue": "database_vault_reveal",
          "frame": 285
        },
        {
          "phrase": "immutable snapshots",
          "cue": "snapshot_tree_glow",
          "frame": 336
        }
      ],
      "wav_path": "/Users/talus/Downloads/youtube_ai/OpenMontage/project_tech/reels/git_18/audio/blocks/git03_truth.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "git04_hashing",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Every file is compressed into a blob named by its SHA-1 hash. Change one word, and only that one hash changes.",
      "start_ms": 12340,
      "end_ms": 18377,
      "duration_ms": 6037,
      "start_frame": 370,
      "end_frame": 551,
      "cues": [
        {
          "phrase": "blob named",
          "cue": "sha1_hash_laser",
          "frame": 425
        },
        {
          "phrase": "only that one hash",
          "cue": "hash_mutation_pulse",
          "frame": 515
        }
      ],
      "wav_path": "/Users/talus/Downloads/youtube_ai/OpenMontage/project_tech/reels/git_18/audio/blocks/git04_hashing.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "git05_pointers",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "The new commit just points to the new blob, while reusing the other 999 old pointers for free!",
      "start_ms": 18437,
      "end_ms": 22959,
      "duration_ms": 4522,
      "start_frame": 553,
      "end_frame": 689,
      "cues": [
        {
          "phrase": "points to the new blob",
          "cue": "commit_tree_repoint",
          "frame": 601
        },
        {
          "phrase": "reusing the other",
          "cue": "shared_pointers_glow",
          "frame": 655
        }
      ],
      "wav_path": "/Users/talus/Downloads/youtube_ai/OpenMontage/project_tech/reels/git_18/audio/blocks/git05_pointers.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "git06_nemi",
      "speaker": "nemi",
      "text": "So Git never duplicates unchanged files \u2014 it's just a tree of hashes! \ud83d\ude0e\u26a1",
      "start_ms": 23019,
      "end_ms": 27051,
      "duration_ms": 4032,
      "start_frame": 691,
      "end_frame": 812,
      "cues": [
        {
          "phrase": "tree of hashes",
          "cue": "nemi_smug_tree",
          "frame": 763
        }
      ],
      "wav_path": "/Users/talus/Downloads/youtube_ai/OpenMontage/project_tech/reels/git_18/audio/blocks/git06_nemi.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "git07_loop",
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "That's how Git branches and merges in milliseconds.",
      "start_ms": 27111,
      "end_ms": 29415,
      "duration_ms": 2304,
